WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.180
I sit in on strategy workshops, review panels and working groups.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.380
Then I write down what actually happens.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.520
Dr Anneke Tolan is an ethnographer of planning at Slop University.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.967
We read thirty-two years of a grazing cooperative's minutes.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:21.297
One item sat in two hundred and thirteen meetings.

00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:22.797
Trees, ongoing.

00:00:23.097 --> 00:00:24.676
It outlived every chair.

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:28.266
She is the University's most cited Senior Research Fellow.

00:00:29.266 --> 00:00:31.170
Nine hundred and fifty-five citations,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.810
an h-index of twenty-five,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.060
and two grants worth more than four hundred and sixty thousand dollars.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.670
I want to know how the future really gets planned.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.728
So I read the minutes.

00:00:43.728 --> 00:00:45.178
Find her work on our website,

00:00:45.328 --> 00:00:46.728
or follow us on Bluesky.
